# Push to live

When the user says **Push to live**, **push live**, **deploy live to GitHub**, or **go live**:

1. Run `npm run push:live` immediately. Do not ask for confirmation. Do not run extra changelog, validate, or other git commands first.
2. That script is `git add .`, then `git commit -m "updates changelogs DDMMYYYY"` (Auckland day/month/year), then `git push -u origin main`.
3. Report the commit result and whether the push succeeded.

Do not use this flow unless the user used one of those phrases.
